msgid "**The shared mechanism is extracted, not duplicated.** `Sampler`, `History`, `record_of`, `judge_answers` and `decide` move into one Python package owned by `svc-ai-s1`, which owns the decider contract, and staged into both `svc-ai-litellm` and `web-svc-translate` the way the MCP adapter's build context is staged per instance. The model router's behaviour MUST not change: its existing tests are the regression net for the extraction."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The strategy derives from the deployment, not from a hand-set value.** `services.translate.router.strategy` follows `services.s1.enabled`: with the decider deployed the gateway asks it, and without it the gateway falls to a `preference` strategy it can compute itself from a declared engine order. One path leads from the deployment to the behaviour."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in `databases.csv`: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**versionen måste passa.** Dumpen säger vilken server den kom ur, i sin egen rubrik - `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` för postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` för mariadb. Det jämförs mot körmotorn innan pre-clean rör någonting. Återställer framåt över en stor version är uppgraderingsvägen och stannar tillåten; bakåt vägras, eftersom en nyare dump använder syntax en äldre server avvisar och schemat skulle redan släppas då. Versionen hålls medvetet inte i `databases.csv`: Den filen är skriven vid frötid och skulle ange den version som distribueras då, inte den dumpen kom från - och en generation kopierad till en annan värd bär sin rubrik längs, en csv rad gör inte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` for postgres, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in ``databases.csv``: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**versionen måste passa.** Dumpen säger vilken server den kom ur, i sin egen rubrik - ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` för postgres, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` för mariadb. Det jämförs mot körmotorn innan pre-clean rör någonting. Återställer framåt över en stor version är uppgraderingsvägen och stannar tillåten; bakåt vägras, eftersom en nyare dump använder syntax en äldre server avvisar och schemat skulle redan släppas då. Versionen hålls medvetet inte i ``databases.csv``: Den filen är skriven vid frötid och skulle ange den version som distribueras då, inte den dumpen kom från - och en generation kopierad till en annan värd bär sin rubrik längs, en csv rad gör inte."

msgid "**Thermals**: one package budget feeds CPU and iGPU. Loading the weak device takes power from the strong one, so \"use every device\" and \"finish soonest\" are different goals on this hardware."
msgstr ""

# vägdes och avvisades här på grund av att filtret i beslut 5 redan lämnar en
# till tre kandidater, så en modell som väljer mellan två som båda kan svara
# köper noggrannhet ingen kan mäta medan du lägger till en behållare, en
# checkpoint och en andra sak som kan vara nere när porten börjar. Operatören
# vände den: [`svc-ai-s1`](../../roles/svc-ai-s1/) Nu tjänar detta beslut
# under beslut 11"S `system_one` strategi.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**This decision was reversed.** A System One *model* was weighed and rejected here on the ground that the filter in decision 5 already leaves one to three candidates, so a model choosing between two that can both answer buys accuracy nobody can measure while adding a container, a checkpoint and a second thing that can be down when the gateway starts. The operator reversed it: [`svc-ai-s1`](../../roles/svc-ai-s1/) now serves that decision under decision 11's `system_one` strategy."
msgstr "**Detta beslut omvändes.** Ett System One *modell* vägdes och avvisades här på grund av att filtret i beslut 5 redan lämnar en till tre kandidater, så en modell som väljer mellan två som båda kan svara köper noggrannhet ingen kan mäta medan du lägger till en behållare, en checkpoint och en andra sak som kan vara nere när porten börjar. Operatören vände den: [`svc-ai-s1`](../../roles/svc-ai-s1/) Nu tjänar detta beslut under beslut 11\"S `system_one` strategi."

msgid "**Three backends ship: LibreTranslate, LTEngine, and Ollama.** LibreTranslate is the default and the only one enabled without further deployment. LTEngine arrives as a new `svc-ai-ltengine` role. Ollama reuses `svc-ai-ollama` and reaches a local model."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Three persona surfaces:** ``guest`` lands on the public landing without a room, ``biber`` and ``administrator`` reach the prejoin lobby behind the SSO gate."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Three persona surfaces:** `guest` lands on the public landing without a room, `biber` and `administrator` reach the prejoin lobby behind the SSO gate."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Three separate counts:** an engine that fails, an engine whose answer is rejected for a mangled protected span, and an engine that loses a comparison are counted apart, and the criteria line of the next decision names each. A failure is counted per engine, a rejection per engine and language pair, so a pair an engine keeps mangling steers the choice away from it without costing it the pairs it serves well. A store that cannot be read is logged and the decision goes on without it."
msgstr ""

