# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tor = compose sidecar**, `network_mode: host`, keys on a named volume, restored from the vaulted mint **before** Tor starts. Backup via `svc-bkp-container-2-local`."
msgstr "**Tor = komponera sidovagn**, `network_mode: host`, Nycklar på en namngiven volym, återställd från den valda mynten **före** Tor börjar. Backup via `svc-bkp-container-2-local`."

msgid "**Tor and direct lists:** ``egress.tor`` and ``egress.direct`` each carry an ``include`` and an ``except``; entries are host names, ``*.`` wildcards, IPs and CIDRs. A host name covers its subdomains, so ``example.org`` and ``*.example.org`` mean the same. ``except`` only narrows its own ``include``, a destination both lists keep takes Tor, and the route decides everything no list matches. ``.onion`` can never be direct."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Tor and direct lists:** `egress.tor` and `egress.direct` each carry an `include` and an `except`; entries are host names, `*.` wildcards, IPs and CIDRs. A host name covers its subdomains, so `example.org` and `*.example.org` mean the same. `except` only narrows its own `include`, a destination both lists keep takes Tor, and the route decides everything no list matches. `.onion` can never be direct."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tor as a first-class deployment axis.** The new *svc-net-tor* role routes onion names through Tor via DNS instead of per-app proxies, offers a chutney flavor for private-net test deployments, and ties its dnsmasq listener to ownership rather than the deploy mode. Applications follow: server-side OIDC discovery and token exchange reach plaintext onion issuers through the SOCKS proxy (WordPress, Joomla, PeerTube, Mobilizon, EspoCRM, Nextcloud), session cookies drop the *Secure* flag where an onion cannot carry it (Taiga, Pixelfed, Joomla), and mail authenticates on the submission port the onion relay actually serves. The deploy matrix gained a tor axis with an onion marker plus enforced and exclusive modes, and lint now requires the onion in every variant. See the [svc-net-tor](roles/svc-net-tor/README.md) README."
msgstr "**Tor som en förstklassig utbyggnadsaxel.** Den nya *svc-net-tor* roll vägar lök namn genom Tor via DNS istället för per-app proxies, erbjuder en chutney smak för privat-net test distributioner, och knyter sin dnsmasq lyssnare till ägande snarare än distribueringsläge. Ansökningar följer: server-side OIDC upptäckt och token utbyte nå klartext lök emittenter genom SOCKS proxy (WordPress, Joomla, PeerTube, Mobilizon, EspoCRM, Nextcloud), sessionscookies släpper *Säker* flagga där en lök inte kan bära den (Taiga, Pixelfed, Joomla), och post autentiserar på inlämningsporten lökreläet faktiskt tjänar. Distributmatrisen fick en toraxel med en lökmarkör plus genomdrivna och exklusiva lägen, och lint kräver nu löket i varje variant. Se [svc-net-tor](roles/svc-net-tor/README.md) README."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Tor image built via `files/Dockerfile`** from a pinned Debian `tor` package (`deb.debian.org`; no sandbox-allowlist change). `deb.torproject.org` = documented alternative requiring an allowlist entry."
msgstr "**Tor bild byggd via `files/Dockerfile`** från en pinned Debian `tor` Paketpaket (`deb.debian.org`; Ingen Sandbox-allowlist förändring). `deb.torproject.org` = dokumenterat alternativ som kräver en bidragslista."

