msgid "**Verification.** Every change passes `make quality-high` and a minimal compose deploy against the running stack: `make compose-deploy apps=<role> variant=0 disable=<every disableable service except design>` (default `initialize` mode, no teardown, single pass, no `full_cycle`). CSS and branding iterations run without a redeploy through `make design-sync app=<role> variant=0` (re-renders shared CSS, role `style.css` and the generated logo assets). A changed `design.js`, task, template or `meta/` file runs through `make compose-role-sync role=<role> variant=0`, which re-runs only the app role against the running stack and renders the CSP hash in the vhost with it. A role pass runs `make test` and the lint targets of the file types it touched after its last edit, and closes with a role sync and the complete role spec; a pass that changed provisioning runs that role sync twice, and the second run reports no change for the tasks it added. `make quality-high` runs once per two or three role passes, at every merge of the main branch and before a role is committed. Each role is also asserted with one further base color, blue `#001f3f`, through `base=` on the sync targets. Swarm verification is out of scope."
msgstr ""

