msgid "The served upstream version moves with every deploy and every role sync: `services.littlejs.ref` in `meta/services.yml` is `main`, and the checkout updates to the head of that branch each run (served during the design pass: commit `8f863c14d114e984a59f42c6ef4b98093581f677`, past the newest tag `v1.25.0`). The role stylesheet maps the thirteen variables of upstream's `examples/style.css`, so an upstream change of that file can undo the mapping without any change in this repository. Options: pin `ref` to a tag such as `v1.25.0`; or pin it to a commit and let the version updater move it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server answers with its input, lightly reworded, often enough that the result keeps every span and every markup character while still being English. Comparing scripts catches it wherever the target does not use the Latin one; for a Latin-script target it would need a language detector."
msgstr "Servern svarar med sin ingång, lätt omordnad, ofta tillräckligt för att resultatet håller varje span och varje markup karaktär samtidigt som det fortfarande är engelska. Jämför skript fångar det varhelst målet inte använder den latinska; för ett latin-skript mål skulle det behöva en språkdetektor."

msgid "The server authenticates against a users file. The role renders it from the directory users whose password is pinned in the inventory (``lookup('users_non_reserved', pinned_only=true)``), so they sign in with their platform username and that password. Bots and accounts with a host login are left out: the host login’s password is the server’s become password and must not reach a third-party form, so the ``administrator`` account renders through a personal account. Passwords are stored as scrypt hashes in the format of the upstream ``passwd.mjs``; the per-user salt is derived from ``secrets.credentials.users_salt_key``, so a rerun writes the same file and only a changed password recreates the container."
msgstr ""

msgid "The server authenticates against a users file. The role renders it from the directory users whose password is pinned in the inventory (`lookup('users_non_reserved', pinned_only=true)`), so they sign in with their platform username and that password. Bots and accounts with a host login are left out: the host login's password is the server's become password and must not reach a third-party form, so the `administrator` account renders through a personal account. Passwords are stored as scrypt hashes in the format of the upstream `passwd.mjs`; the per-user salt is derived from `secrets.credentials.users_salt_key`, so a rerun writes the same file and only a changed password recreates the container."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server needs an active browser tab and plugin connection, and can execute powerful design-context operations."
msgstr "Servern behöver en aktiv webbläsarflik och plugin-anslutning och kan utföra kraftfulla designkontextoperationer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment's credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Servern börjar med en token från distributionens referensbutik, binder till behållarnätverket och publicerar ingen port. Kontroller på plats är avstängd och något ursprung accepteras, eftersom den som ringer är en tjänst på samma nätverk som presenterar token snarare än en webbläsare som bär en cookie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment’s credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Servern börjar med en token från distributionens referensbutik, binder till behållarnätverket och publicerar ingen port. Kontroller på plats är avstängd och något ursprung accepteras, eftersom den som ringer är en tjänst på samma nätverk som presenterar token snarare än en webbläsare som bär en cookie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server's own thread count follows the CPUs its container may use, which a deploy decides; only the client side is free to vary per run. This sweeps it against real catalog entries and records the winner for the env builder, so a tuned host keeps its numbers across every `make dotenv`."
msgstr "Serverns egen trådräkning följer CPU: erna dess behållare kan använda, som en utplacering bestämmer; endast klientsidan är fri att variera per körning. Detta sveper det mot riktiga katalogposter och registrerar vinnaren för env-byggaren, så en tuned värd håller sina nummer över varje `make dotenv`."

msgid "The service block that pulls the provider into the inventory and makes the service loader preload it."
